Assignment-1: Fixture Management API

This project is a Node.js RESTful API for managing sports fixtures, built with Express and Sequelize (PostgreSQL).

Features

- Create, read, and delete fixtures
- Unique fixture codes
- Fixture status tracking (scheduled, ongoing, finished, cancelled)
- Uses Sequelize ORM and migrations

Project Structure

```
.
├── app.js
├── package.json
├── .env
├── .gitignore
├── config/
│   ├── config.js
│   └── database.js
├── controller/
│   └── fixtureController.js
├── middleware/
├── migrations/
│   └── 20250905081356-create-fixture.js
├── models/
│   ├── fixture.js
│   └── index.js
├── routes/
│   └── fixtureRouter.js
├── seeders/
└── Readme
```
 Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the root directory with the following content:

```
PORT=3000
ENV=development

DB_USERNAME=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=taku
DB_DATABASE=assignment_db
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_DIALECT=postgres
```



1. Clone the repository

   
   git clone https://github.com/TakuSlyDube/Assignment-1.git
   cd Assignment-1
   

2. Install dependencies

   
   npm install
   

3. Configure your `.env` file (above)

4. Run migrations

   ```sh
   npx sequelize-cli db:migrate
   ```

5. Start the server


   npm run start


   The API will run on `http://localhost:3000` by default.


All endpoints are prefixed with `/api`.

- `POST   /api/fixtures`  
  Create a new fixture

- `GET    /api/fixtures`  
  Get all fixtures

- `GET    /api/fixtures/:fixture_code`  
  Get a fixture by its unique code

- `DELETE /api/fixtures/:fixture_code`  
  Delete a fixture by its unique code



json body
{
  "fixture_code": "ABC123",
  "home_team": "Team A",
  "away_team": "Team B",
  "fixture_date": "2024-06-10",
  "fixture_time": "15:00:00",
  "venue": "Stadium Name",
  "league": "Premier League",
  "status": "scheduled"
}


